{
 "comment": "loans_interest questions at the reference's current head, an individual whose previous-year turnover is a placeholder below both limits, activity not recorded (not a deductor, but unknown as a placeholder): an expense credited to a loan and its reversal, asked about as the lender's charge (Charge Loan, with its interest over the threshold); an entry against only another loan's interest ledger (Misposted Loan); a bank debit and its return by identical narration, one by a number in the credit's reference, and a repeated narration (Pair Loan); a repayment past the balance, then a cash loan tested on its own amount, then one the two walks disagree on, listed as not computed (Walk Loan); a repayment reportable under both walks and flagged only under the second (Flag Loan); a Government loan taken, reported, and repaid, not (Govt Loan); one lender on two ledgers whose names match only case-folded (Strasse A, B); two ledgers with no lender (Nameless A, B); and the notices: a loan left out of the list, instalments to a creditor in three months, and no notice for suspense in two months, a duties ledger, a bank OD or a ledger whose group chain is incomplete, though it reaches Loans (Liability).",
